# tasks/data holds the deployment records (deployed.json, accountlayer.json,
# deployment-report.json, archived checkpoints). Ignoring the whole directory meant the
# only off-chain record of a mainnet deployment lived on one machine — and verify:all,
# which reads these files, could never run from a fresh clone. Deployed addresses are
# public on-chain, so they are tracked. Only the in-progress checkpoint is transient.
tasks/data/*/checkpoints/checkpoint-*.json
tasks/data/checkpoints/checkpoint-*.json
tasks/data/*/verify-failed.json
tasks/data/verify-failed.json
# Local/simulated chains — not worth tracking.
